{"Time":"2026-10-08T13:38:23.021430413Z","Action":"output","Package":"github.com/system-inc/adamic/stage1/cohere/lint","Test":"TestMutants/nexus-for-in-message","Output":"          no-var  This is a `var` declaration, which is function-scoped and hoisted rather than block-scoped. The binding exists from the top of the enclosing function, so it is readable above the line that declares it and it leaks out of the block it looks like it belongs to: a `var` inside an `if` is still in scope after the `if` ends. A `var` in a loop is one binding shared by every iteration, which is why a closure created in the loop sees the final value rather than its own. Use `let`, or `const` when nothing reassigns it.\n"}
